            {
                "entry_id": "d8d4e98e-0b0e-319a-b91b-52dc7469f86d",
                "word": "rosâtre",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "206ec116-99c4-4cc0-9fb0-915295f3db67",
                        "entry_id": "d8d4e98e-0b0e-319a-b91b-52dc7469f86d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "rosâtres"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1713cd56-06ba-3a69-8b7e-96ada7f71bbc",
                        "entry_id": "d8d4e98e-0b0e-319a-b91b-52dc7469f86d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui a une teinte rosée, d’un rose sale."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e4e5876-ded6-4d68-bd30-77f8da8e7789",
                                "sense_id": "1713cd56-06ba-3a69-8b7e-96ada7f71bbc",
                                "text": "Une table carrée, d’un merisier plus rosâtre que le reste de l’ameublement, à dessus de marbre gris, grillagée de cuivre, était en face du lit, contre le mur, entre la fenêtre et la porte d’un grand cabinet de toilette."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "112f397f-ea3f-4ec1-b322-c962c621caff",
                                "sense_id": "1713cd56-06ba-3a69-8b7e-96ada7f71bbc",
                                "text": "Il portait un chandail rosâtre et ses joues trop fardées tournaient au lie de vin."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6c95c4a-09c2-4600-b282-f6d07ef1e5be",
                                "sense_id": "1713cd56-06ba-3a69-8b7e-96ada7f71bbc",
                                "text": "Quant à l'ambiance, elle est faite de visions terrifiantes, de hurlements de douleur, de dégueulis rosâtres, de vomissements d'injures, de transpirations gluantes, de gémissements épouvantables, de pourrissements vivants, de râles atroces, de décompositions lentes et de morts qui n'en finissent plus..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ab02e7b-295a-4d00-a93b-91fbbb545c4e",
                                "sense_id": "1713cd56-06ba-3a69-8b7e-96ada7f71bbc",
                                "text": "Sa peau était rosâtre et si douce que tous les hommes rêvaient de la frôler ne fût-ce que du revers des doigts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8334a32e-2989-4de3-8764-3f19ec4bb69d",
                                "sense_id": "1713cd56-06ba-3a69-8b7e-96ada7f71bbc",
                                "text": "La sporée, abondante à la fin de maturité, paraît poudrer les lamelles d’une couleur crème rosâtre."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "545cf67f-6010-4f3d-9eb4-4635c426d723",
                        "source_entry_id": "d8d4e98e-0b0e-319a-b91b-52dc7469f86d",
                        "source_sense_id": "1713cd56-06ba-3a69-8b7e-96ada7f71bbc",
                        "target_lang_word": "pinkish",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pinkish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b5282f2-c5ab-3f89-802a-cd043fafc1cd",
                                        "entry_id": "ee2a4ef5-caf3-34e2-b389-11847532da72",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Somewhat pink."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfbc826a-dc29-421c-9bed-7fa6d5af6260",
                                                "sense_id": "7b5282f2-c5ab-3f89-802a-cd043fafc1cd",
                                                "text": "Sepia Delft tiles surrounded the fireplace, their crudely drawn Biblical scenes in faded cyclamen blending with the pinkish pine, while above them, instead of a mantelshelf, there was an archway high enough to form a balcony with slender balusters and a tapestry-hung wall behind."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "643416de-ec38-4142-b9c9-b7506877a80f",
                                                "sense_id": "7b5282f2-c5ab-3f89-802a-cd043fafc1cd",
                                                "text": "West Quantoxhead, 1½ miles to the south-west, has some handsome houses and an imposing mansion, St Audries - now a girls' school - built in the Tudor style in the 19th century, at the same time as the pinkish-buff stone Church of St Ethelreda - also called St Audrey - which has an elegant tapering spirelet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3a68abc-27db-4a04-a2cf-0fc38461245e",
                                                "sense_id": "7b5282f2-c5ab-3f89-802a-cd043fafc1cd",
                                                "text": "F[eatures] [...] Black or dark brown back; faded white stripes and white patches on the sides; pinkish/peach-colored belly"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "267f8674-9d11-4e63-9e75-29bc013a724e",
                                                "sense_id": "7b5282f2-c5ab-3f89-802a-cd043fafc1cd",
                                                "text": "While some of the more exotic varieties are becoming more popular with nationwide growers, such as the pale pinkish white pineberry, local farms will frequently plant a few different varieties to best suit their region."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dd92d06c-7a31-40f3-b309-fa5bf1bac71e",
                        "source_entry_id": "d8d4e98e-0b0e-319a-b91b-52dc7469f86d",
                        "source_sense_id": "1713cd56-06ba-3a69-8b7e-96ada7f71bbc",
