                                                "sense_id": "8f77d67b-cf01-30aa-bd93-4df24fa0f8eb",
                                                "text": "Two flags of color rosied the jut of his cheekbones, giving him an unexpectedly boyish look."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7f63116-7268-3d03-98b3-2ffe5f589017",
                                        "entry_id": "be9b99a1-9c9b-3cfa-bfd6-4ac681fffd53",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To present in a deceptively optimistic or positive light."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca337c96-47f2-4bfc-ac12-107edf8922f5",
                                                "sense_id": "d7f63116-7268-3d03-98b3-2ffe5f589017",
                                                "text": "In suburban Kent, the owners of the Chislehurst Caves recognised their potential as communal shelters. Nottingham people used the caves under the castle. Retrospect has rosied the accounts of shelter life."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
